<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Misirlou, surf-rock instrumental by Dick Dale</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1962</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Pulp Fiction, film</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1994</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Dick Dale's recording on the soundtrack</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Pump It (Black Eyed Peas)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2006</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sampled</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Misirlou (the Beach Boys, on Surfin' U.S.A.)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1963</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover version, after Dale</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Misirlou, jazz arrangement by Nick Roubanis</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1941</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">English-language song by Chaim Tauber, Fred Wise and Milton Leeds</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Misirlou (Harry James)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1941</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Misirlou (Jan August)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1946</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">French-language version (Darío Moreno)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1951</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Misirlou, Greek-American folk dance</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1945</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody, slowed, for the Syrtos dance</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Akh, Anoushes / Ah Anoush Yar (Reuben Sarkisian)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">early 1950s</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Armenian words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Lela Vranjanka (Staniša Stošić)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1972</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Serbian version</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Arabic folk version played on the oud by Dick Dale's uncle</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the source of Dale's arrangement</span></li></ul></section>
